\cf0 \
	The STR# resource format used to store many of the strings in Nova may seem to be incompatible with the flexible nature of plugin files. For example, a plugin for a new ship would have to replace several of the built-in STR# resources to incorporate its new name into the game. The problem arises when you want to use two plugins that try to modify the same STR# resource.\
\
	The solution is not to change the STR# resources at all, but to use Nova\'d5s handy string patching functionality by updating only select strings in a STR# resource by providing Nova with a properly-numbered 'STR ' resource. For example, to change the first cargo type from food to something else, you\'d5d simply create a 'STR ' resource with the ID 9000 and type in the name of your new commodity. A chart of 'STR ' resource numbers is provided below:\
\

\f2\i \ul String Type:								Replacement 'STR ' ID range:
\f1\i0 \ulnone \
\cf2 Message buoys							1000-2500\cf0 \
\
Hail quotes								5000-5511\
\cf2 \
Stellar types								7000-7063\cf0 \
\
Base prices of commodities					9300-9305\
\cf2 \
Commodity abbreviations for status display		9400-9405\cf0 \
\
Govt-specific greetings for comm dialog		10000-12559 (first 10 for \
govt -1, second 10 for govt 0, third 10 for govt 1, etc.)\
